  "rule": "If the anthracnosis notice is active because of water stress (Ks < 1 on more than half of the last 28 days) the irrigation priority becomes \"protect the crop\" (price 1 day of stress avoided) whatever the grower stated; roya-only or no notice leaves the priority as stated. Approved in principle by the owner.",
  "decision": "irrigate 20 mm today if the predicted stress days avoided (exported network web/data/coffee_ptc_mlp.json, seed 29) exceed the price (3 days = save water, 1 day = protect the crop); the FAO-56 rule irrigates when the capped running depletion exceeds p = 0.40 of the available water and does not use the priority, so the notice rule cannot change it",
  "noticeDays": "days in t+1..t+30 with the anthracnosis notice active by stress (share of Ks<1 days over the last 28 days > 0.5), recomputed day by day from the soil water balance with and without the 20 mm irrigation at the end of day t (neverIrrigate/alwaysIrrigate are the two counterfactual series; the policy rows pick the one its decision leads to, per scenario)",
  "rainAndMinador": "Roya \"favorable\" and minador \"probable\" days in t+1..t+30 depend only on the weather, not on irrigation; they are reported next to the anthracnosis days and do not change any decision.",
  "modes": {
   "saveWater": "priority stated = save water, price 3",
   "protectCrop": "priority stated = protect the crop, price 1",
   "saveWaterWithNoticeRule": "priority stated = save water, raised to protect the crop when anthracnosis-by-stress is active at the decision day"
  },
  "caveat": "Notices are information with a source, not damage predictions; the number of notice days is a measure of water stress, not of disease. Scenarios of different shade/soil at one site-year share the weather."
 },
